  "reviewed_by": "Claude focused review for turn write amplification",
  "reason": "The change moves write-once turn request snapshots, sealed turn reasoning and goal skill instructions into content-addressed chat_snapshot_parts beside their rows, folds the step ledger incrementally, validates entity updates once, saves routing prose with the step's usage write, stores the answer and turn completion in one transaction (adopting an answer an earlier Core stored), and runs bounded workspace provenance off the event loop. The selection covers the new regression module (per-step write bytes/reads, parts lifecycle and integrity, goal skills, killed-Core crash windows, provenance loop and bounds, storage update, ledger fold), the provider chat/tool loop, prompt-cache replay, context pruning, throughput ledger, goals, schedules, decisions, queue, subagent and agent-message flows, hooks and hook turn ends, workspace provenance, storage, deletion, export/import, reconnection, catch-up, temporary chats, media, workspace and the goal/skill/hook/pending-turn API paths.",
  "exclusions": "Full suites are not approved and are excluded. Files red on pristine origin/main eadae6a are selected by node, excluding exactly their 51 pre-existing failures (identical on this branch): test_chat.py (restart/stream/claim regressions from #559 that P1 claude/resume-admission is fixing), test_chat_subagents.py and test_harness_provider_subagents.py (P1/P3), test_chat_api.py, test_chat_final_synthesis_recovery.py, test_native_hook_turn_ends.py, test_tool_catalog.py, and test_chat_leftovers.py (pre-#559 red). No frontend, Playwright or native code changed; the API response shape is unchanged except goal skill entries carrying part_id instead of instructions, which the UI never read. No schema migration: the new entity kind uses the existing entities table.",
